      <div class="card" style="border-color:#42A5F5;"><h3 style="color:#42A5F5;">💧 Water Pollution</h3><div class="divider"></div>
        <p><strong style="color:var(--xp);">Definition:</strong> Water pollution occurs when harmful substances enter rivers, lakes, oceans, or groundwater.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;"><strong style="color:var(--xp);">Causes:</strong> Plastic waste, chemical runoff, sewage, and improper disposal of waste near waterways.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;"><strong style="color:var(--xp);">Effects:</strong> Harms aquatic life, affects drinking water quality, and impacts communities that depend on water.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;"><strong style="color:var(--xp);">Prevention:</strong> Proper waste disposal, recycling plastics, reducing chemical use, and protecting water bodies.</p>
