    <div style="padding:20px; max-width:800px; margin:0 auto;">
      <div class="card" style="border-color:#A1887F;"><h3 style="color:#A1887F;">🌱 Soil Pollution</h3><div class="divider"></div>
        <p><strong style="color:var(--xp);">Definition:</strong> Soil pollution occurs when harmful substances contaminate the land, reducing its quality for plants, animals, and agriculture.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;"><strong style="color:var(--xp);">Causes:</strong> Improper waste disposal, plastic, chemical contamination, batteries and e-waste, and excessive agricultural chemicals.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;"><strong style="color:var(--xp);">Effects:</strong> Harms soil organisms, reduces agricultural productivity, and can affect the quality of food and groundwater.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;"><strong style="color:var(--xp);">Prevention:</strong> Proper waste management, recycling, reducing plastic use, using waste bins, and protecting green areas.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;"><strong style="color:var(--xp);">What you can do safely:</strong> Don't litter, use bins, reduce plastic, care for gardens. If you find hazardous waste, tell a trusted adult.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;"><strong style="color:var(--xp);">Fun fact:</strong> ✨ A single teaspoon of healthy soil contains billions of microorganisms that help plants grow and keep the ecosystem balanced!</p>
        <button class="btn btn-soil" style="margin-top:16px;" onclick="showScreen('soil')">🎮 Explore Soil World →</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="tab-content" id="learn-tab-recycle">
    <div style="padding:20px; max-width:800px; margin:0 auto;">
      <div class="card" style="border-color:#66BB6A;"><h3 style="color:#66BB6A;">♻️ Waste & Recycling</h3><div class="divider"></div>
        <p><strong style="color:var(--xp);">What is recycling?</strong> Recycling means turning used materials into new ones instead of throwing them away. It reduces waste and protects natural resources.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;"><strong style="color:var(--xp);">What can be recycled?</strong> Paper, cardboard, glass bottles, plastic containers, metal cans, and electronic items (through special facilities).</p>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;"><strong style="color:var(--xp);">What about hazardous waste?</strong> Batteries, electronics, chemicals, and medicine should NEVER be thrown in regular bins. Ask a trusted adult how to dispose of them properly in your area.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;"><strong style="color:var(--xp);">Fun fact:</strong> ✨ Recycling one aluminium can saves enough energy to power a TV for approximately 3 hours!</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="tab-content" id="learn-tab-ecosystems">
    <div style="padding:20px; max-width:800px; margin:0 auto;">
      <div class="card" style="border-color:#FFA726;"><h3 style="color:#FFA726;">🌳 Ecosystems</h3><div class="divider"></div>
        <p><strong style="color:var(--xp);">What is an ecosystem?</strong> An ecosystem is a community of living organisms — plants, animals, insects, fungi, and microorganisms — interacting with their environment.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;"><strong style="color:var(--xp);">Why do they matter?</strong> Healthy ecosystems provide clean air, clean water, food, medicine, and many other services we depend on.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;"><strong style="color:var(--xp);">How does pollution affect ecosystems?</strong> Pollution can disrupt food chains, reduce biodiversity, and make ecosystems less able to recover from other pressures.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;"><strong style="color:var(--xp);">Fun fact:</strong> ✨ Bees pollinate about one-third of the food we eat. Protecting the environment helps protect bees and the food systems they support!</p>
