      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="tab-content" id="learn-tab-protection">
    <div style="padding:20px; max-width:800px; margin:0 auto;">
      <div class="card" style="border-color:var(--accent);"><h3 style="color:var(--accent);">🌎 Environmental Protection</h3><div class="divider"></div>
        <p><strong style="color:var(--xp);">Who is responsible?</strong> Protecting the environment is a shared responsibility. Governments, organizations, communities, families, and individuals all play important roles.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;"><strong style="color:var(--xp);">What do governments do?</strong> Governments create environmental laws, manage protected areas, and regulate pollution from industry and agriculture.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;"><strong style="color:var(--xp);">What can young people do?</strong> Learn about environmental issues, make responsible daily choices, care for local environments, and encourage others to do the same.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;"><strong style="color:var(--xp);">Important:</strong> Never try to clean up hazardous or chemical waste on your own. Always involve adults for anything potentially dangerous.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:10px;"><strong style="color:var(--xp);">Fun fact:</strong> ✨ The word "ecology" comes from the Greek word "oikos" meaning home. Earth is our home — and protecting it protects us all!</p>
